.TH FL-USERS 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.8" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-users \- user accounts and login screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-users\fR [\fBusers\fR|\fBlogin\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Users and Login Screen pages of \fBfl-settings\fR(1) as a program of their
own, for systems that do not use the rest of fldesktop. \fBUsers\fR adds,
removes and changes the accounts of people (full name, administrator,
password, picture, groups, automatic login with greetd). \fBLogin Screen\fR
sets up \fBfl-greet\fR (style, background, the list of users).
.PP
The changes are made as root by \fBfl-settings-helper\fR through pkexec, so
an administrator password is asked (polkit actions
\fBorg.fldesktop.settings.users\fR and \fBorg.fldesktop.settings.login-screen\fR).
The argument names the tab to open.
.PP
In an fldesktop session the same pages are in Settings, so the menu entry is
hidden there.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-settings\fR(1), \fBfl-greet\fR(1)
